// REJECTS: Field 'ownership' is required
//
// A MemSqlFunction with no `ownership`. The grammar makes it optional -- memSqlFunction's body
// is a `( ... )*` alternation, as every activator's is -- and MemSqlFunctionTreeWalker calls
// validateAndExtractRequiredField for it.
//
// The point of the fixture is the ASYMMETRY, not the requirement. BigQueryFunction's grammar
// is the same grammar with the words changed: same fields, same order, same optionality in the
// .g4, same `stage` rule that nothing references, same DeploymentConfiguration element. And
// BigQueryFunctionTreeWalker calls validateAndExtractOPTIONALField for `ownership`. So
//     BigQueryFunction fixture::bq::stage { functionName: '...'; function: ...; }
// parses (it is in ../fixtures/t2-bigquery.pure) and the identical MemSqlFunction below does
// not.
//
// Nothing short of reading both walkers reveals this, and a rewrite that shares one activator
// implementation between the two vendors -- the obviously correct engineering call -- gets one
// of them wrong whichever way it chooses.
###MemSql
MemSqlFunction fixture::neg::NoOwnership
{
   functionName : 'demoFunction';
   function : zxx(Integer[1]):String[1];
   description : 'no ownership';
}
